<div class="wrap page-head"><h1>Submit a manuscript</h1><p class="lede">En Route welcomes submissions that contribute to the Catholic intellectual and spiritual tradition: theology, philosophy, spirituality, literature, poetry, biography, and children's books, from established and emerging authors alike.</p></div>
<section class="band" style="padding-top:1.5rem">
  <div class="wrap two-col top">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Before you submit</h2>
      <p>Manuscripts must be complete and professionally edited. Submit in Microsoft Word (.doc or .docx). Include a cover page with the title, your full name, mailing address, phone number, and email address.</p>
      <p>If your work includes illustrations, you must provide them. If it includes copyrighted material, you are responsible for securing permissions.</p>
      <h2>Editorial expectations</h2>
      <p>We expect submissions to be carefully prepared and polished. Authors are responsible for professional editing before submission; if that is out of reach, run the manuscript through Grammarly first. Strong manuscripts show clarity and coherence, proper grammar and structure, and faithfulness to Catholic teaching where it applies.</p>
      <h2>Publishing model</h2>
      <p>En Route is a traditional publisher. We assume the cost of preparing your book for publication. You receive a 10 percent royalty on retail sales and may purchase copies at a 40 percent discount. Books are printed on demand and sold through Amazon and wholesale, and our authors are invited onto WCAT Radio.</p>
      <p>Your first ten copies are free with your initial order. Discerning En Route? <a class="textlink" href="https://enroutebooksandmedia.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/En-Route-Contract-Template-071126.docx">Download the contract template</a>.</p>
      <h2>Your platform</h2>
      <p>Many authors begin without an established platform, and that is fine. We expect you to promote your work and to build a public presence where you can. Every author takes part in at least one interview on WCAT Radio. Other opportunities include reviews, speaking engagements, media appearances, and bookstore events.</p>
      <h2>Scripture and Church texts</h2>
      <p>Up to 5,000 words of Scripture (NABRE), the Catechism, and the Lectionary may be used without permission. Liturgical texts (ICEL) require notification. Securing every other permission is the author's responsibility.</p>
      <h2>Good to know</h2>
      <p>Submission does not guarantee acceptance. Publishing timelines vary with the production queue; authors who are ready and engaged tend to move through it faster.</p>
      <p>Send your manuscript to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="steps" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.4rem">
        <div><h3>1. Send it</h3><p>Complete manuscript in Word, with the cover page, to {{ site.email }}.</p></div>
        <div><h3>2. We read it</h3><p>Every submission is read. You'll hear back.</p></div>
        <div><h3>3. We prepare it</h3><p>Design, typesetting, and formats for print and Kindle, at our cost.</p></div>
        <div><h3>4. It's published</h3><p>Paperback and Kindle, often hardback and Audible, listed on Amazon and available wholesale.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a class="btn" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Manuscript%20submission">Email your manuscript</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
